+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:16",
+   "text": "So this is one of the"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:17",
+   "text": "most satisfying cuts when you pull it off right."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:20",
+   "text": "It's called a match cut."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:21",
+   "text": "And it connects two shots using something visually similar."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:25",
+   "text": "So that could be a shape or subject in the same position within the frame."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:30",
+   "text": "And it's kind of a way to say that these two things belong together."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:35",
+   "text": "So it can link moments in time or places, or you can use it to create metaphors"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:41",
+   "text": "I really use this when I want to show a connection"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:43",
+   "text": "between things, like a past version of me turning it to the present one,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:47",
+   "text": "or to have a smooth transition between two completely different scenes."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:51",
+   "text": "...that I wanted to be a YouTuber just like half of the world today."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:55",
+   "text": "And if you're matching people, there's one trick that's"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:57",
+   "text": "really important to remember, and it's that you try to match the eye position"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:01",
+   "text": "across the cut."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:02",
+   "text": "Because when the eyes stay"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:04",
+   "text": "in the same place on the screen, the transition will feel way more natural."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:07",
+   "text": "So, try using a match cut next time to intentionally connect two things"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:12",
+   "text": "that mean something together."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:15",
+   "text": "You know, sometimes the most important part of a cut"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:18",
+   "text": "is when it's actually happens."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:20",
+   "text": "Editing is rhythm."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:22",
+   "text": "And if your video moves at the same pace the whole time,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:25",
+   "text": "your audience will sure start to tune out."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:28",
+   "text": "So paying attention to the speed of your cuts"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:30",
+   "text": "is how you keep them engaged by shifting the tempo."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:33",
+   "text": "The faster cuts here are building tension, and the slower cuts"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:36",
+   "text": "are there to let something land emotionally."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:41",
+   "text": "it's all about contrast."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:43",
+   "text": "Just like music, it needs climax, and it needs a release."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:46",
+   "text": "And I use this when I want to change the energy of a scene or guide the viewer"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:50",
+   "text": "into how I want them to feel: exciting or calm or emotional or chaotic."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:55",
+   "text": "And if your video feels too flat or too chaotic, try"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:59",
+   "text": "playing with the speed of your cuts."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:01",
+   "text": "It's really one of the easiest ways to shape emotion. And you know..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:05",
+   "text": "the truth is, editing is always a bit of a puzzle, and there's"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:09",
+   "text": "always a point where it feels like it's not going to work."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:12",
+   "text": "But I want you to know that that's really normal,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:14",
+   "text": "because if you're hitting a wall, it probably means that you're close"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:17",
+   "text": "to something special or something meaningful."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:20",
+   "text": "And if you do want some help from start to finish, if you're unsure"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:23",
+   "text": "what to shoot or how to shape a story that's actually flows."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:27",
+   "text": "That's exactly why I created the Story Starter Kit."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:30",
+   "text": "it gives you a simple, repeatable storytelling method."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:33",
+   "text": "You will write your story with clear templates,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:35",
+   "text": "Plan your shots with the visual guide, and then move into the edit with confidence"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:38",
+   "text": "using my pre-built editing templates and a step by step video walkthrough."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:43",
+   "text": "and I also just upgraded the kit with the 7-Cuts Guide."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:47",
+   "text": "It's a seven page guide"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:48",
+   "text": "with a summary and extra information about the seven cuts in this video,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:52",
+   "text": "so the link is in the description if that sounds helpful."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:54",
+   "text": "And one last tip before we wrap up."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:57",
+   "text": "You don't need to cram all these seven cuts into one video."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:01",
+   "text": "Just ask yourself, what does this moment need?"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:04",
+   "text": "Does it need a smooth flow, a surprise, or a shift in rhythm maybe?"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:08",
+   "text": "And just pick the cut that serves that moment best."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:12",
+   "text": "From there, you can always build further."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:14",
+   "text": "Now if you want to learn how to shape that story"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:16",
+   "text": "from the very beginning, check out this video next where"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:19",
+   "text": "I'll walk you through the 5-line story method that I use to write every script."
+  }
+ ],
+ "key_techniques": [
+  "flow_cut",
+  "smash_cut",
+  "jump_cut",
+  "action_cut",
+  "wide_medium_close",
+  "match_cut",
+  "pacing_cut",
+  "eye_position_match"
+ ]
+}
\ No newline at end of file
