+{
+ "title": "The ONLY 5 Editing Secrets You Need to Tell Any Story (Tim Runia)",
+ "source": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dhpazqW_OaU",
+ "duration_sec": 914,
+ "transcript": [
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:00",
+   "text": "So you had this great idea for a video."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:05",
+   "text": "You wrote your script."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:06",
+   "text": "Planned your shots."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:07",
+   "text": "And actually got out in the wild filming those shots."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:10",
+   "text": "And now you're finally ready to edit."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:12",
+   "text": "But now everything falls apart."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:15",
+   "text": "Should I use this shot?"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:16",
+   "text": "Am I cutting too soon?"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:17",
+   "text": "Where should this go?  - Why does it feel off? - What am I doing!?"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:20",
+   "text": "Of course."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:21",
+   "text": "Because editing can be the most overwhelming part of filmmaking."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:25",
+   "text": "but I've been editing for over 15 years, and today..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:28",
+   "text": "I’m sharing some of my most valuable editing tricks.."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:31",
+   "text": "that will make the difference between a bunch of clips stacked together.."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:34",
+   "text": "and a story that actually flows."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:36",
+   "text": "And that will feel good."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:38",
+   "text": "Just like that first time when you had that idea."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:41",
+   "text": "Now let's get into it."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:45",
+   "text": "What I want to share here..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:46",
+   "text": "are the editing choices that actually make your story flow."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:49",
+   "text": "Things that keep people watching because they want to..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:52",
+   "text": "and because they lean into your story."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:54",
+   "text": "These are simple but powerful secrets."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:56",
+   "text": "And even if you only use one of them, your videos will already feel stronger."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:00",
+   "text": "And also, stick around to the end,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:01",
+   "text": "because I will share one bonus tip that took me way too long figure out."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:05",
+   "text": "But once I did, it really made my editing way faster and less stressful."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:10",
+   "text": "So here's the first secret that completely changed my process."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:14",
+   "text": "Back when I started, I would shoot everything..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:17",
+   "text": "and then I would dive straight into the edit and just try to make things work."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:21",
+   "text": "And every time my timeline was a mess."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:23",
+   "text": "so after many painful re-edits, I realized this: that your voice over, your music"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:28",
+   "text": "and even your sound effects are way more important than most people think."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:32",
+   "text": "So now I start my edits with only audio before I touch a single clip."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:36",
+   "text": "Yeah, you really heard that well."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:37",
+   "text": "But believe me, it will really change your edits."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:40",
+   "text": "So here's how I do it: for YouTube..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:42",
+   "text": "I record my hook and my intro voiceover before I even start shooting."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:47",
+   "text": "then I find music that matches the energy that I have in my head,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:50",
+   "text": "and I will even add a few sound effects And right away I see where my voice over"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:53",
+   "text": "is too long, where things don't work, or where I should work on the pacing."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:57",
+   "text": "and even better..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:58",
+   "text": "It always gives me new inspiration and new ideas for shots."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:02",
+   "text": "And because I haven't shot anything yet, I can still add those shots to my shotlist."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:06",
+   "text": "For example, in this video, I did exactly that,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:09",
+   "text": "Laying down my voice over with music showed me that my voice over was too long"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:14",
+   "text": "That build-up can be much quicker..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:16",
+   "text": "Because I don't need 7 seconds to explain  that we're overwhelmed."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:21",
+   "text": "We can do that much quicker."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:22",
+   "text": "And the rhythm of the track that inspired me to do that paper toss scene on the beat."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:28",
+   "text": "And another great thing about this is that once you've shot everything,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:31",
+   "text": "the edit is already halfway done because the pacing is there,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:35",
+   "text": "the voiceover is there, and the music is there."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:37",
+   "text": "So the only thing you basically have left to do is add the shots in."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:40",
+   "text": "So ,the next video you're working on, lock in your audio first,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:43",
+   "text": "because you will spot some time issues instantly."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:46",
+   "text": "And the more you do this, you know, the more your brain will practice"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:50",
+   "text": "creating a story in your head before even filming."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:52",
+   "text": "And that actually is one of the most useful skills"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:55",
+   "text": "you can build as a filmmaker."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:58",
+   "text": "If there's one thing"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:59",
+   "text": "that makes or breaks your video, it's pacing."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:02",
+   "text": "Your edit’s speed is your storytelling pulse."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:05",
+   "text": "And I think it’s one of the biggest mistakes that I see even from experience editors."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:09",
+   "text": "It's that they're staying in the same pace for too long."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:13",
+   "text": "So here are three things that I think really shape pacing."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:16",
+   "text": "The first one is shot length because short and snappy"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:18",
+   "text": "cuts make things fast or increase the tension, and longer shots"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:22",
+   "text": "are more for emotion or producing calmness."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:26",
+   "text": "Then the second one is shot motion."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:28",
+   "text": "You have chaotic handheld movements that can really add energy,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:33",
+   "text": "or smooth and stable frames that really calm things down."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:36",
+   "text": "And I think mixing those in the right way can be really strong."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:40",
+   "text": "And then there's a third,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:41",
+   "text": "which is music and sound, because your soundtrack really sets"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:44",
+   "text": "the heartbeat as well you know..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:45",
+   "text": "A driving beat really pushes the story forward"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:48",
+   "text": "and softer music is really what can let it breathe as well."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:52",
+   "text": "And of course, sometimes..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:54",
+   "text": "a silence can be really strong as well."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:58",
+   "text": "Anyway, if you keep the pace high the entire time,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:01",
+   "text": "people will get overwhelmed."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:02",
+   "text": "And if it stays slow, they will get bored."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:05",
+   "text": "So yeah, it's really good to time that change and energy."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:09",
+   "text": "Because that really snaps the attention back..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:11",
+   "text": "or it really puts people in the right emotion when you want to."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:16",
+   "text": "For example, listen to the first 30 seconds of this video."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:19",
+   "text": "We start with no music."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:21",
+   "text": "tension rising with a sound effect, then pause for a second,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:25",
+   "text": "then full energy, quick shots, fast music,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:31",
+   "text": "then a short break, a longer shot."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:33",
+   "text": "Tension is building again."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:35",
+   "text": "Then energy back up with fast cuts."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:39",
+   "text": "Then we release into slower shots and no music."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:42",
+   "text": "Finally we settle into a neutral pacing. And that variation is really"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:45",
+   "text": "what keeps a hook like that really alive."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:48",
+   "text": "So the next time you edit, just spend a little more time on pacing."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:51",
+   "text": "Just mark your big moments and your quiet moments,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:54",
+   "text": "and then let your cuts, your movements, and your music flow between them."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:58",
+   "text": "Your audience..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:59",
+   "text": "They will stick with you much longer. I'm sure."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:03",
+   "text": "you know,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:03",
+   "text": "one of the hardest things, but also one of the most important things"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:06",
+   "text": "about editing is finding music that actually fits the mood of your story."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:11",
+   "text": "You really don't want to know"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:12",
+   "text": "how much time I spent on tweaking music in my edits, just so it fits perfectly."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:16",
+   "text": "But sometimes you wish you could just tweak a song a bit..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:19",
+   "text": "..maybe take out the vocals or take out the guitar."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:22",
+   "text": "Well, you can do that now because Audiio released Elements 2.0 a while ago"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:27",
+   "text": "and it's a really huge upgrade because now you can separate every part of the track"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:32",
+   "text": "the vocals, the drums, the bass, piano,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:35",
+   "text": "guitar... even the strings, all in studio quality."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:38",
+   "text": "So for me, that means that I can take a track that I already love."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:41",
+   "text": "Just strip it down completely, or build it back up with all those different pieces"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:46",
+   "text": "and that just makes it really much easier to adjust the music"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:49",
+   "text": "to whatever fits the rhythm or the pacing that I'm looking for."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:53",
+   "text": "So if you want to try that out, go explore Elements 2.0 and get 70% off"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:57",
+   "text": "your first year of Audiio Pro at audiio.com/timrunia"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:02",
+   "text": "using the code at checkout."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:04",
+   "text": "And of course you'll find the link in the description as well."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:08",
+   "text": "So when I first started out creating videos,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:11",
+   "text": "once I got to the editing process, before I knew it, I would spend two days"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:15",
+   "text": "perfecting the first 30s, you know, adding sound effects or maybe already color grading..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:21",
+   "text": "And I would totally forget what I was making."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:24",
+   "text": "But then I discovered the power of the assembly edit."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:27",
+   "text": "And that's basically"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:27",
+   "text": "like sketching before you paint, or outlining a book before you write."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:32",
+   "text": "It's all about getting a rough shape down first and then start refining."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:36",
+   "text": "So if you've already created the hook and the intro of your video"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:40",
+   "text": "with an audio blueprint..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:41",
+   "text": "then you can use the assembly edit to shape the rest of your story fast."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:45",
+   "text": "So here's how I do it."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:47",
+   "text": "First, I spot the footage that tells the story."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:49",
+   "text": "So spotting just means cut out the junk and keep the clips you will actually use."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:54",
+   "text": "Then I drag some of them into the timeline in the rough story order,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:58",
+   "text": "with a beginning, a middle, and an end."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:00",
+   "text": "And I'm not polishing anything yet."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:01",
+   "text": "If I already recorded my voiceover, I will drop that in too."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:04",
+   "text": "And then I spent time finding music that matches the pace."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:07",
+   "text": "You know, sometimes"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:08",
+   "text": "it’s temporary music, but sometimes I can already find the real track."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:12",
+   "text": "Then I just play everything back from the beginning to the end,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:15",
+   "text": "and I can really watch the rough story unfold."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:18",
+   "text": "And I just really pay attention and immediately"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:20",
+   "text": "I will see where the gaps are, the pacing feels off,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:24",
+   "text": "or what kind of shots I'm still missing, or sometimes what I can really get rid of."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:28",
+   "text": "So before you dive into polishing, build your assembly edit."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:32",
+   "text": "Drag your key clips into a story order and then refine after that."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:36",
+   "text": "It will save you hours of frustration"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:38",
+   "text": "and I'm sure it will give you way more clarity on where your edit is heading."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:42",
+   "text": "And where your story is heading."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:45",
+   "text": "So with my first edits..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:46",
+   "text": "I loved picking a song and just cutting on the beat."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:49",
+   "text": "We've all probably done those edits and they feel nice,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:53",
+   "text": "but it gets repetitive pretty fast."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:57",
+   "text": "And I think real flow goes way deeper."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:00",
+   "text": "So here are just a few ways to create flow."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:02",
+   "text": "The first one cut intentionally."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:05",
+   "text": "Don't just throw clips together."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:07",
+   "text": "Just think about where the eyes of your audience"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:10",
+   "text": "are on the screen and how the movements of the eyes"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:14",
+   "text": "flow from one shot to the next, or how one shot flows to the next."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:19",
+   "text": "Then the second one is beat accents, because instead of cutting on the beat,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:23",
+   "text": "you can land an action with the beat like when you're dropping something,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:29",
+   "text": "or when you're stepping in a frame, or even raising an eyebrow..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:33",
+   "text": "I will show you an example in a bit."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:35",
+   "text": ", Then the third audio transitions."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:37",
+   "text": "Because a sound effects across two shots can really glue them together."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:42",
+   "text": "And sometimes a sound effect does that even much better than the shots themselves."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:48",
+   "text": "And a combination is even better."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:50",
+   "text": "So, for example, in the intro of this video,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:52",
+   "text": "I cut the movement going out of the shot from the right to the left."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:57",
+   "text": "Then coming in from the right to the left."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:59",
+   "text": "So it feels fast but smooth."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:01",
+   "text": "Then I hit beat accents."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:03",
+   "text": "Me coming on to the desk or raising my eyebrows right on the beat."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:07",
+   "text": "So instead of cutting on the beat, the action itself matches the beat."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:16",
+   "text": "So next time you edit..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:17",
+   "text": "don't just think about speed, think about movements."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:19",
+   "text": "Where are the eyes going? Where's the rhythm pulling?"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:22",
+   "text": "Just try one intentional cut, maybe one beat accent and one audio transition."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:27",
+   "text": "And I'm sure your edit will feel much..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:30",
+   "text": "smoother instantly."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:34",
+   "text": "if your edit feels predictable, people tune out."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:36",
+   "text": "And that's why I like to break my own rhythm with a quick sudden cut..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:40",
+   "text": "or a change of scene, or just something completely unexpected."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:43",
+   "text": "So that contrast, that's really what can bring people back"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:48",
+   "text": "into your story, even a small surprise creates a little spike of focus."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:52",
+   "text": "And those tiny spikes are really what keep people watching."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:56",
+   "text": "As long as it's not too forced and it's part of your story"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:01",
+   "text": "You can use contrast..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:02",
+   "text": "This can be anything, loud versus quiet"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:05",
+   "text": "or fast versus slow"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:07",
+   "text": "or bright versus dark"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:08",
+   "text": "Or, I add suprise."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:10",
+   "text": "Just something playful or something abrupt that no one saw coming."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:16",
+   "text": "For example, in this video's hook,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:18",
+   "text": "I froze the frame"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:19",
+   "text": "and dropped in text before you expected it because it was like in the first three seconds..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:24",
+   "text": "and that tiny break already made you pay much more attention."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:28",
+   "text": "And then later I cut to silence when I'm at the empty desk and that sudden"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:32",
+   "text": "shift in energy that instantly makes you think, hey, what just happened there?"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:38",
+   "text": "But really try to make it a part of the story."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:40",
+   "text": "So in your next edit, just try to find one spot to add contrast or surprise."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:45",
+   "text": "Maybe it's a freeze frame or a quick silence or an unexpected cut."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:49",
+   "text": "You really don't need many of those."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:51",
+   "text": "But you know, really, one well-placed surprise can already make your"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:55",
+   "text": "story pretty unforgettable."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:57",
+   "text": "You know, editing will always be a puzzle."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:00",
+   "text": "No matter how many tricks you learn, how many secrets you learned,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:03",
+   "text": "there will always be these moments where it feels like"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:06",
+   "text": "things are not going to work."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:07",
+   "text": "And that's really normal because filmmaking is really hard."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:12",
+   "text": "But when your story finally comes together in the edit, it's always worth it."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:16",
+   "text": "But if you find it hard to finish your own videos,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:20",
+   "text": "check out my Story Starter Kit, the link’s in the description."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:23",
+   "text": "And I really designed this to make filmmaking simple and take you"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:26",
+   "text": "from staring at a messy timeline to finally finishing a video you’re proud of."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:31",
+   "text": "The link is in the description and it's the most affordable way to finally finish, I think,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:36",
+   "text": "and get your ideas out of your head onto the screen."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:39",
+   "text": "Now, my last bonus secrets is “be ruthless”."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:43",
+   "text": "when I started out editing, I could spend days trying to squeeze"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:47",
+   "text": "in every shot that I filmed just because I filmed the shot and the shot was nice,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:52",
+   "text": "but now I really try to make my selections really fast."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:56",
+   "text": "Kill Your Darlings is how they call it, and it's really true."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:59",
+   "text": "You will have to say goodbye to a lot of great shots,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "12:02",
+   "text": "but the faster you will learn to cut what doesn't serve the story,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "12:06",
+   "text": "the more energy you will have to shape the story itself."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "12:09",
+   "text": "that's also where the assembly edit from earlier really helps,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "12:11",
+   "text": "because it really forces you to make decisions quickly."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "12:14",
+   "text": "And the more ruthless you are, the better edits will be."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "12:18",
+   "text": "And now that you've got all this fresh knowledge to dive into your edit..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "12:21",
+   "text": "check out this video next"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "12:23",
+   "text": "where I will show you the kind of cuts you need to apply this into your edits."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "12:28",
+   "text": "Good luck!"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "12:30",
+   "text": "You can do it!"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "12:32",
+   "text": "Go edit, edit that thing."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "12:56",
+   "text": "No matter how many tricks or secrets you know, there will always be a moment"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "12:59",
+   "text": "where it feels like it's not going to work."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "13:02",
+   "text": "And that is normal because filmmaking is hard."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "13:04",
+   "text": "But when a story finally comes together, it's always worth it."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "13:08",
+   "text": "if you find it hard to start and finish your own story"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "13:11",
+   "text": "straight from video, be sure to check out my Story Starter kit."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "13:14",
+   "text": "Because it's the science to make filmmaking simple and take you from"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "13:18",
+   "text": "staring at a blank timeline to actually finishing a video that you're proud of"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "13:23",
+   "text": "gives you a simple structure to turn an ID into a clear story,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "13:26",
+   "text": "plan your shots without overthinking, and edit smoothly"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "13:29",
+   "text": "until you hit export the links in the description."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "13:33",
+   "text": "I think it's a really affordable way to finally get your ideas out of your"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "13:37",
+   "text": "head and onto the screen,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "14:51",
+   "text": "You know, editing is always a puzzle."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "14:52",
+   "text": "No matter how many tricks or secrets you learn,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "14:55",
+   "text": "there will always be moments that it feels like it's not going to work."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "14:59",
+   "text": "And that's normal because filmmaking is hard."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "15:01",
+   "text": "But when the story finally comes together, it's always worth it."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "15:05",
+   "text": "And if you find it hard to even start or finish your own story driven videos,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "15:09",
+   "text": "check out my story start a Case because it's designed to."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "15:14",
+   "text": "Yeah. Hello?"
+  }
+ ],
