@@ -0,0 +1,1269 @@
+{
+ "title": "21 Mistakes That Kill Your Video (Tim Runia)",
+ "source": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oiNnWm8Z5l4",
+ "duration_sec": 976,
+ "transcript": [
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:01",
+   "text": "So, this is the part where I usually create an engaging hook and tell you"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:06",
+   "text": "all about my filmmaking experience and why you should listen to me."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:09",
+   "text": "But today, I'm just going to dive straight in, and tell you all about"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:18",
+   "text": "You know, when I started out, all I was focused on"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:21",
+   "text": "was getting beautiful shots, lens flares, shallow depth of field."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:25",
+   "text": "And when you put that all together, it sure looks beautiful"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:27",
+   "text": "and it can be good enough to enjoy watching,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:30",
+   "text": "but it can also feel completely empty because story..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:34",
+   "text": "That's really what makes people care"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:35",
+   "text": "and a good story can make average footage feel really magical."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:39",
+   "text": "But a bad story can really make the perfect shot feel completely meaningless."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:43",
+   "text": "So focus on the story."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:46",
+   "text": "Filmmaking is already pretty hard,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:50",
+   "text": "so my advice would be to not make it harder."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:53",
+   "text": "That's something that I was very good at,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:55",
+   "text": "I always thought, I had to make things more complicated,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "0:58",
+   "text": "to give it more meaning and to make it feel more professional."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:01",
+   "text": "But most of the time, really, the simple version is the best version."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:05",
+   "text": "Especially when you just start out, you know"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:07",
+   "text": "the audience really doesn't care how complex your setup was."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:10",
+   "text": "They really care about how you made them feel."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:13",
+   "text": "So really think about, are you complicating things"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:16",
+   "text": "because the story needs it, or just because you think you have to?"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:20",
+   "text": "There's a really big difference."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:23",
+   "text": "They say that a film is made"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:24",
+   "text": "three times when you write it, when you shoot it, and when you edit it."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:28",
+   "text": "And it's so true because early on I used to completely panic"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:32",
+   "text": "when my shoot didn't go exactly as planned."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:34",
+   "text": "But now I kind of expect it because that's just how it goes every time."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:38",
+   "text": "no matter if you're shooting solo"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:40",
+   "text": "or you're directing a big film, you have to be able to adapt on set."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:44",
+   "text": "That's really part of the job, and it's also what makes it fun."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:47",
+   "text": "You know, it's also the creative part of it."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:49",
+   "text": "So if you just let go a little, the film usually gets better"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:52",
+   "text": "and so do you as a filmmaker."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:56",
+   "text": "It is very tempting"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "1:57",
+   "text": "that once you start shooting to keep shooting, I'm very guilty of this,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:01",
+   "text": "especially when I'm shooting abroad, because planning is usually harder,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:04",
+   "text": "and when you get a little bit uncertain it feels like"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:08",
+   "text": "it's more safe to just film everything, but let me tell you, it's not because more"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:13",
+   "text": "footage doesn't make your story better, it just makes the editing take forever."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:18",
+   "text": "So try to shoot with intention."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:20",
+   "text": "because if you know why you're filming something, you will shoot less, but"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:24",
+   "text": "you will be able to tell more with the footage that you have."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:28",
+   "text": "on the flip side, sometimes you think you've got the shots"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:31",
+   "text": "after just one shot,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:32",
+   "text": "and then you go to the edit and you're stuck"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:34",
+   "text": "because there's no different angle to cut to."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:36",
+   "text": "if you want to make this as simple as it gets, go for a wide, a medium and a close."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:42",
+   "text": "Always."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:42",
+   "text": "It's filmmaking 101, but it makes your edits"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:44",
+   "text": "look instantly more professional and it gives you the options"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:47",
+   "text": "when you're piecing the story together later in the edit."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:50",
+   "text": "And it's really nice to have that."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:52",
+   "text": "It might not always be the most fun part, but it really is"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:55",
+   "text": "one of the most important ones."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:57",
+   "text": "Create your shotlist."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "2:59",
+   "text": "Improvising feels really fun until you sit down in the edit"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:02",
+   "text": "and realize that nothing connects."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:04",
+   "text": "And believe me, I've done full shoots where I forgot to film one key moment"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:09",
+   "text": "and suddenly I'm trying to stitch"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:10",
+   "text": "the whole story together with random B-roll and crazy editing tricks."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:14",
+   "text": "Fix it in post."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:15",
+   "text": "That's how we call it. But it's not fun."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:17",
+   "text": "And you don't need a huge plan."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:19",
+   "text": "Just a few notes or a simple shotlist makes the whole process much smoother."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:24",
+   "text": "So this really is why you want to create a shotlist and to make it easier for you."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:27",
+   "text": "Last month I created a tool with which you can easily create shot"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:31",
+   "text": "lists on your desktop or on your phone or sync together."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:35",
+   "text": "And then you can export the list to PDF,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:37",
+   "text": "or just use it on your phone to take off the shots as you go."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:40",
+   "text": "There's also a bit of help and guidance, and it's for each shot,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:43",
+   "text": "and it's free to use for the most part."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:44",
+   "text": "And if you want a full version, that's part of the Story Starter Kit,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:47",
+   "text": "but the free version will really get you far enough."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:51",
+   "text": "You don't need another tutorial."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:53",
+   "text": "You need a project because a project forces you to learn and practice"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "3:58",
+   "text": "and to face problems, to make mistakes and to figure things out along the way."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:02",
+   "text": "And that is when theory actually clicks inside of your head."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:05",
+   "text": "And of course you will still watch tutorials, but this time they are to"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:09",
+   "text": "to fix specific problems inside your project instead of random tips"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:14",
+   "text": "like this video."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:15",
+   "text": "So yeah, I guess don't watch more videos like this after this one of course."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:20",
+   "text": "But seriously, every project you finish teaches you ten times more,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:24",
+   "text": "at least than any tutorial ever could."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:29",
+   "text": "At one point, I went through something that I call my zoom transition era"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:32",
+   "text": "because every other shots"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:33",
+   "text": "had a creative transition in it, especially those hyper zoom transitions."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:38",
+   "text": "back then, it wasn't a lot of work to create those yourself."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:40",
+   "text": "But now there are so many plug ins and it's really easy to do,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:44",
+   "text": "and it may feel creative, but most of the time it's just noise."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:48",
+   "text": "Clean cuts usually tell the story much better."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:51",
+   "text": "So yeah, really try to make those do the talking and not all those"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:54",
+   "text": "plug ins and fancy editing transitions."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "4:59",
+   "text": "Especially when you're just starting out..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:00",
+   "text": "You will learn way faster and become a much better storyteller"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:04",
+   "text": "and filmmaker without those."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:08",
+   "text": "It is"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:08",
+   "text": "so easy to get caught up in the flow of shooting that you just assume"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:12",
+   "text": "that everything looks and sounds fine,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:14",
+   "text": "and then you come home, you drop it in the edit and you realize that one shot is"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:18",
+   "text": "out of focus, or the mic was recording too loud, or you mixed up words."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:22",
+   "text": "And I've done that too many times."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:24",
+   "text": "And to be honest, it still happens sometimes."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:26",
+   "text": "Also with these YouTube videos."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:28",
+   "text": "But if you can..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:29",
+   "text": "just take a minute between setups or when you're changing gear"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:33",
+   "text": "to just check the playback. Zoom in."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:35",
+   "text": "Just listen back and just make sure it's all there,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:37",
+   "text": "because that will really save you from bumping your heads into your desk later."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:43",
+   "text": "So about 8 year ago, I was moving to Amsterdam."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:46",
+   "text": "And I know this is insanely stupid that I put all my camera gear together"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:51",
+   "text": "with my hard drive full of client footage in a box"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:54",
+   "text": "in this net that we pull up three stories high."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "5:57",
+   "text": "But that's just how people move places in Amsterdam."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:00",
+   "text": "So of course you can guess what happened."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:03",
+   "text": "The box fell out, and my completely new gh4"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:06",
+   "text": "with lenses and everything and a hard drive fell down."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:10",
+   "text": "And I still don't know how exactly, but the camera itself and the lenses,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:15",
+   "text": "they all survived..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:15",
+   "text": "I think because the hard drive was on the bottom,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:19",
+   "text": "so the hard drive didn't survive."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:21",
+   "text": "And you will only have to learn this lesson once, most people will learn it"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:25",
+   "text": "the hard way. So let me tell you this once."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:28",
+   "text": "Back up your footage twice because you will"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:32",
+   "text": "be forever grateful when something happens."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:34",
+   "text": "And of course, never put your hard drives in a net."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:38",
+   "text": "That was so &amp;^# stupid."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:41",
+   "text": "Probably every filmmaker, learns this lesson"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:43",
+   "text": "that great visuals with bad sound is unwatchable."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:48",
+   "text": "You can shoot on your phone from 2015, and things are fine if the audio is good."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:53",
+   "text": "But the moment that someone can't hear you properly, they instantly click away."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "6:57",
+   "text": "So really be sure to check your audio before you start recording."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:00",
+   "text": "And also in the edit."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:01",
+   "text": "Spent enough time on balancing it out and listen to it on different devices"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:05",
+   "text": "just to be sure that it sounds good enough."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:08",
+   "text": "So yeah, sound is really a big part of your story."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:10",
+   "text": "And that's why I care a lot about the tools that I use for it."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:13",
+   "text": "And this video is sponsored by Audiio."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:15",
+   "text": "They've just released LinkMatch 2.0."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:18",
+   "text": "It's a rebuilt version of their music"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:20",
+   "text": "matching tool that makes finding the right soundtrack way easier."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:24",
+   "text": "You can drop in any song link that you like from Spotify or YouTube,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:28",
+   "text": "for example, and it will instantly give you similar tracks from their library."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:32",
+   "text": "So if you already know the kind of vibe you want,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:34",
+   "text": "it really helps you to find something that fits fast."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:37",
+   "text": "You can even refine it by a specific part of the song, like the intro"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:41",
+   "text": "or the chorus, and it shows you exactly which section matches your reference."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:45",
+   "text": "if you want to try it out for free, go to audiio.com/linkmatch."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:49",
+   "text": "And if you decide to get the full version, use my link...."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:51",
+   "text": "Audiio.com/timrunia and the code “Tim"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:55",
+   "text": "Runia” to get 70% off your first year of Audiio Pro."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "7:58",
+   "text": "Now let's go to the next mistake"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:02",
+   "text": "if your timeline looks like a"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:03",
+   "text": "big spaghetti mess, I really get it because it can become extremely chaotic."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:08",
+   "text": "And when I was starting out, I didn't think it mattered that much."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:12",
+   "text": "I thought it was pretty cool with all these layers."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:14",
+   "text": "But once you start editing longer projects, organization becomes everything,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:18",
+   "text": "especially when you're a bit chaotic."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:20",
+   "text": "And most creative people are."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:21",
+   "text": "So yeah, use color codes to structure name your sequences properly"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:26",
+   "text": "and just find full structures that work for you."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:29",
+   "text": "Creating these habits will really make editing feel much smoother and way"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:33",
+   "text": "less stressful, because your brain can now stay focused on the creative parts"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:37",
+   "text": "instead of constantly having to search for stuff."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:41",
+   "text": "And that's much better."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:42",
+   "text": "So create that habit."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:45",
+   "text": "The best filmmakers are good editors."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:48",
+   "text": "A lot of people think editing is just the boring part, and that it's necessary."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:52",
+   "text": "And I understand why,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:53",
+   "text": "because sometimes editing can feel very repetitive, very frustrating."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "8:57",
+   "text": "But editing is not the finishing touch."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:00",
+   "text": "It's really where the story comes alive."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:01",
+   "text": "So for me, I've always loved editing, and it's always been"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:05",
+   "text": "the part where I really find the story."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:08",
+   "text": "You know, random shots start to make sense, or the metaphors"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:11",
+   "text": "that I thought of in the script really come alive, and the music does"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:14",
+   "text": "its job perfectly, and that's really the magic of it."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:17",
+   "text": "So if you start to hate editing, please remember"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:21",
+   "text": "that it's not just post-production, it's really story creation."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:25",
+   "text": "And the better you can imagine your edit before"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:26",
+   "text": "you start filming, the easier it will be as a filmmaker."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:30",
+   "text": "So go practice."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:33",
+   "text": "So yeah, I think that there's this phase that every filmmaker"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:36",
+   "text": "goes through trying to make videos that look like everyone else's."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:39",
+   "text": "Because you copy other creators, you copy their shots, you use the same LUTs..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:43",
+   "text": "And of course, this is fine because it can teach you a lot, but it is very possible"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:48",
+   "text": "that one day you suddenly realize that it doesn't feel like you."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:52",
+   "text": "Now, I don't think you have to be original on purpose, but just following"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:56",
+   "text": "what you really find beautiful, that really develops your own taste,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "9:59",
+   "text": "you know you can really use your own taste as your compass."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:02",
+   "text": "Because that is what eventually will make you stand out from the crowd,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:06",
+   "text": "your own taste."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:07",
+   "text": "So follow it."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:10",
+   "text": "Most people fall into this trap, and it's really a problem"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:12",
+   "text": "because most beginners want their first video"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:14",
+   "text": "to look like some sort of cinematic short film that only more"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:17",
+   "text": "experienced people can make, so then they never finish."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:20",
+   "text": "Especially if you're someone who's starting out."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:22",
+   "text": "Or maybe if you're"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:23",
+   "text": "someone who does have experience but is starting to create a different"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:26",
+   "text": "kind of video, you know, maybe you're starting"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:28",
+   "text": "in front of the camera for the first time because you're doing YouTube"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:31",
+   "text": "or you're acting or whatever..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:33",
+   "text": "your first video isn’t"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:34",
+   "text": "supposed to be perfect."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:36",
+   "text": "It's really not."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:37",
+   "text": "And the faster you finish one project, the faster you will grow."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:41",
+   "text": "Really, believe me."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:44",
+   "text": "I've seen this happen so many times, even to people who are really good."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:47",
+   "text": "A friend of mine who I share this office space with."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:50",
+   "text": "He shot all this beautiful footage for a documentary is creating"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:54",
+   "text": "and it's really amazing stuff."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:55",
+   "text": "But then suddenly client work took over"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "10:59",
+   "text": "and months went by and I know that's just how it goes."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:03",
+   "text": "And yes, I'm talking to you, Ruben..."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:05",
+   "text": "And I really get it."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:06",
+   "text": "It's happened to me so many times as well."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:08",
+   "text": "And that's just how it goes."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:10",
+   "text": "But what I've learned is that"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:11",
+   "text": "if you want to keep a project alive, you need to keep momentum,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:15",
+   "text": "even if it's just 15 minutes a day or two hours a week."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:19",
+   "text": "You know, just selecting a few good clips or writing a sentence for the voiceover."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:24",
+   "text": "It doesn't really matter what it's all about."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:26",
+   "text": "Keeping a project inside your head, because once you stop completely,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:30",
+   "text": "it all fades out of your mind very quickly."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:32",
+   "text": "And the difference between finishing something and"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:35",
+   "text": "abandoning it completely,"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:38",
+   "text": "is just usually staying connected to it long enough"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:41",
+   "text": "to give it a push across the finish line."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:45",
+   "text": "Yeah."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:46",
+   "text": "So this one's really painful because I did it for years myself as well."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:50",
+   "text": "I would spend weeks working on something and then it would be ready"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:54",
+   "text": "and I would convince myself that it wasn't ready or that it wasn't good enough."
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "11:58",
+   "text": "But let me tell you that nothing will ever be ready, and nothing will"
+  },
+  {
+   "timestamp": "12:02",
+   "text": "especially not be good enough."
+  },
+  {
